Syndicate Development backup system — SPEC-017 Phase 2
======================================================

Source of truth: deploy/backup/ in the application repository. Everything in
/usr/local/bin and /etc/systemd/system here is installed by deploy/backup/install.sh.
Edit the repo, re-run the installer; do not hand-edit the installed copies.

Full documentation: docs/deployment/ovh-server-access.md, "Backups" section.

Files
-----
  /usr/local/bin/syndicate-backup          nightly dump + archive + upload
  /usr/local/bin/syndicate-backup-verify   weekly "is this still running" check
  /usr/local/bin/syndicate-backup-alert    OnFailure= handler, emails via Resend
  /usr/local/bin/syndicate-backup-drill    restore rehearsal into a scratch database
  /etc/syndicate-backup/backup.env         which tier is backed up (no credentials)
  /etc/syndicate-backup/alert.env          Resend key + from/to addresses
  /etc/syndicate-backup/rclone.conf        R2 token, installed by hand

Everyday commands
-----------------
  systemctl list-timers 'syndicate-backup*'
  journalctl -u syndicate-backup.service -n 50
  systemctl start syndicate-backup.service        # run one now
  syndicate-backup-drill                          # rehearse a restore

Installing rclone.conf by hand
------------------------------
The R2 token is never committed and never placed in a Docker volume. Create it in
the Cloudflare dashboard scoped to Object Read & Write on the syndicate-backups
bucket only, then:

  sudo install -d -m 0700 /etc/syndicate-backup
  sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root /dev/stdin /etc/syndicate-backup/rclone.conf <<'EOF'
  [r2]
  type = s3
  provider = Cloudflare
  access_key_id = <access key id>
  secret_access_key = <secret access key>
  endpoint = https://<account id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
  region = auto
  acl = private
  no_check_bucket = true
  EOF

no_check_bucket is required, not optional: a bucket-scoped token cannot HeadBucket,
and rclone's default pre-flight check would fail every upload with AccessDenied.
